; Print "<object> is <state>" for the object in IX
;
; Loads the first name phrase (+8) of the record in IX and falls into $A172.
; .
; $A172 picks the state word for the id in A from #R$A224 (bit 7 clear:
; unlocked, empty, off, closed, dead) or from #R$A234 (bit 7 set: locked, full,
; broken, on, open, alive), indexed by the id without bit 7, and prints
; "<the phrase> is <word>." with #R$AFBB. The commands use it to say why they
; failed ("The door is locked.") or what they did ("The goblin is dead.").
; .
; Hardware: none (the text goes through the message printer).
;
; A State id (bit 7 selects the second word table)
; IX Record of the object (not used at $A172)
; HL Name phrase of the object ($A172 only)
; Preserves DE.
@label=PrintStateIX
c$A16C LD L,(IX+$08)
 $A16F LD H,(IX+$09)
; This entry point is used by the routine at #R$A164.
@label=PrintStateHL
*$A172 PUSH DE
 $A173 PUSH HL
 $A174 LD HL,$A224   ; table of the ids without bit 7
 $A177 BIT 7,A
 $A179 JR Z,$A17E
 $A17B LD HL,$A234   ; bit 7 set: the other table
*$A17E CALL $A0BD    ; DE = state word
 $A181 POP HL
 $A182 PUSH DE
 $A183 PUSH HL
 $A184 LD HL,$AFBB   ; <the_arg> is <word>.
 $A187 CALL $72DD
 $A18A POP DE        ; restore DE
 $A18B RET
